# Windows batch files must be pure CRLF in the working tree: cmd.exe's label search
# (`call :label`, `goto`) misreads LF-only lines at some byte offsets, and the launcher
# is also started by the in-app updater. The index already stores them as LF, so this
# rule needs no renormalization; it only fixes what checkout writes (autocrlf=false
# clones and source zips included). tests/test_line_ending_policy.py guards the bytes
# (CRLF, BOM-less UTF-8, chcp 65001 before any non-ASCII byte and before `type`ing the UTF-8 crash log).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
